                            <comment id="16736499" author="ilyak" created="Mon, 7 Jan 2019 23:54:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=dpavlov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;dpavlov&quot;&gt;dpavlov&lt;/a&gt; Even if encoding is consistent between nodes, it might lead to data corruption when Unicode strings are encoded to 8-bit encoding and then de-encoded. Some characters will turn into ?&apos;s as they&apos;re not representable in a given 8-bit charset. Therefore, we should keep the warning. They may still run but they need to be aware. We have quite a few warnings anyway which are printed even with default configuration.&lt;/p&gt;

